<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Charles VII, Holy Roman Emperor</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1697">1697</a>–<a href="/years/1745">1745</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Charles Albert of Bavaria</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Charles VII, born Charles Albert, was Elector of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a> from 1726. On the death of Charles VI he refused to accept <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maria-theresa">Maria Theresa</a>'s succession and, with French support, was elected <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-emperor">Holy Roman Emperor</a> in 1742, the first non-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> in three centuries. Austrian troops occupied Bavaria during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-austrian-succession">War of the Austrian Succession</a>, and he died in 1745.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/charles-vii-holy-roman-emperor.jpg" alt="Charles VII, Holy Roman Emperor" width="320" height="461" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Workshop of Georg Desmarées · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Carl_Albrecht_VII_by_workshop_of_George_Desmarees,_M%C3%BCnchner_Residenz.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
